## New Capabilities Identified

- **PeakFlames Design System adoption** — vendor the design system's token CSS
  (11 files: `styles.css` + 10 `tokens/*.css`) byte-identical into the repo (source:
  the already-verified copy in the sibling `summit` repo, originally from design
  project `11ea476f-926c-40ea-8d34-91522c12d907`) and import it as the base stylesheet
  layer.
- **Additive `.pf-*` component styling** — apply the system's component classes
  (`pf-btn`, `pf-card`, `pf-tabs`/`pf-tab`, `pf-label`, `pf-input`, `pf-error`,
  `pf-hint`) alongside existing class names in the `src/ui/` components, with zero DOM
  or behavior change; existing tests are the regression baseline.
- **Brand typography** — Archivo / IBM Plex Sans / JetBrains Mono via Google Fonts
  (`@import` in vendored tokens + `preconnect`), mirroring the reference
  implementation.
- **Visual-discipline TORs** — dark obsidian canvas + brand type ramp; exactly one
  flame-accented element per view; visible keyboard focus rings; ember-gradient
  selected-filter treatment. These become a new `05-visual-design` requirements feature
  file and a design-system epic.

## Priority Signal

This is the final deliverable of the inter-repo Summit competition: adopt the PeakFlames
Design System "in the same way" the sibling `summit` repo did (its epic R5e7z3Y is the
reference playbook). Priority is fidelity to that playbook — byte-identical vendoring,
additive-only class changes, and the same four visual-discipline TORs — applied to this
repo's own file layout (`src/styles.css`, `src/ui/*`). The MVP functionality already
shipped (5/5 epics complete) must not regress.

## Deferred Items

- Theme toggle / light mode — explicitly not wanted; the brand canvas is dark-first.
- Self-hosting the brand fonts — rejected for this cycle in favor of mirroring the
  co-worker's Google Fonts approach (may revisit if a strict zero-network guarantee is
  ever required).
- Any redesign beyond restyling — no DOM structure, copy, or feature changes.
